  "rationale": "O12 (N2, docs/CASESTUDY.md) on M3, the typed extracted Rollup: a successful challengeState adds proofWindow W to the finalize deadline of every other unfinalized batch (Rollup.sol:485-495) and records the challenger's deposit (msg.value); setPause(true) then deletes the open challenge and credits the deposit back to the challenger (Rollup.sol:575-583), but keeps the extensions, so the cancellation (challengeState, setPause) does not restore the state: I71's L_undo_cancel_Rollup_challengeState_setPause is REFUTED. Both residues are the protocol's design. The contract bounds the residue of one cancellation as intended, locally (the I64 C_t64_ext shape): from any reachable state s, after a successful challengeState x and a successful setPause y, each batch's finalize deadline moved by at most W (read in s), its commit time did not move, and the challenger's claimable reward grew by at most x's msg.value. Every quantity is read as a Nat (N), so the bound cannot wrap; the code's checked arithmetic makes each stored sum the exact Nat sum on every successful step.",
